Z||000004||WKDFIRO||04-14-2001||06:31 AM||||I would highly recommend the first site on "onfire's" list. I haven't checked out the others but that Iron Duke site is the one I used in one of my articles for my club's newsletter. Very informative and VERY realistic. <P>180 hp without SD parts...not really realistic...<P>140 is about the top realistic end without compromising too much for the street. Like it says on the site, the Iron Duke is supposed to be economical, not hi-performance. ||||reg||6
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||04-15-2001||05:15 PM||||There are plenty of duke performance parts<BR>out there if you know where to look.<P>Fiero Conversions makes a turbo,<BR>several companies make headers,<BR>IRM makes a dual exhuast,Comp<BR>Cams makes a pretty radical cam, MSD<BR>makes a box and dist. for them, and<BR>even GM still sells the alum. Super Duty<BR>cyl. head, the Fiero store sells the Holley<BR>big bore T-body and perf. eng. kit.<BR>Uumm....did I make my point. :-)<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
